# The humanAlways path list, owned by `merge.humanAlways` in .claude/workflow.json, which
# points here from `merge.humanAlwaysLedger` (docs/standards/architecture.md rule 9; #440).
# Adding or removing a member moves three carriers: CLAUDE.md § Workflow copies the list,
# merge-pr.sh § classify computes with it, and merge-pr.test.sh case 6b asserts one member
# against the live list. The other carriers name the list by reference ("a humanAlways
# path"), so a member change leaves them true; they move only if the key is renamed.
# Inside the owner, merge.humanAlwaysRule gives one reason per member and moves with it.
owner: .claude/workflow.json
claim: the paths whose PRs wait for the owner's review before merging, whatever their file type, unless merge.approvedAtPlanRule or merge.amendmentRule exempts the PR
cite: humanAlways
sweep: \bhumanAlways|\.claude/ledgers/human-always-paths\.ledger
carrier: CLAUDE.md
carrier: .claude/scripts/merge-pr.sh
carrier: .claude/scripts/merge-pr.test.sh
carrier: .claude/skills/review-loop/SKILL.md
carrier: .claude/skills/run-issue/SKILL.md
carrier: .claude/skills/plan-issue/SKILL.md
carrier: .claude/agents/ticket-agent.md
carrier: .claude/agents/task-orchestrator.md
carrier: .claude/agents/planner.md
carrier: .claude/scripts/check-no-network-egress.sh
carrier: .claude/scripts/fill-verdict.sh
carrier: .claude/scripts/adr-amendment-check.mjs
carrier: .claude/scripts/adr-amendment-check.test.sh
carrier: docs/adr/README.md
carrier: .github/workflows/ci.yml
excluded: docs/review-feedback.md
excluded: docs/friction-log.md
excluded: docs/tech-debt.md
